    "narrative": "Today\u2019s projections favor **Mickey Moniak** (75.33) and **Brice Turang** (73.74) as the engines of the Ghost Ride the WHIP offense. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Logan Webb; the projection indicates a significant +14% park factor and a +14% platoon edge, making him our premier play despite the solid pedigree of the opposing starter. Similarly, **Brice Turang** earns his spot at the top of the board due to a favorable matchup against J. Cabrera, where his projected efficiency is buoyed by a +16% SP skill advantage and the expected stability of the #3 spot in the lineup. **James Wood** also remains a tier-one starter (73.57) due to his elite 0.418 xwOBA, though he carries a slight penalty for facing a tough catching arm behind the plate.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer was keeping **Kyle Karros** (45.99) on the bench. While **Kyle Karros** benefits from the same park boost as **Mickey Moniak**, his lower order placement and restricted platoon upside kept his efficiency score below our active threshold. Furthermore, **Josh Naylor** (45.59) was considered, but his unfavorable matchup against Dylan Cease\u2014combined with a poor BvP history\u2014made him the odd man out in a crowded utility and corner infield landscape. We are keeping a close watch on **Jose Caballero** (60.52); while he ranks as a strong start, the 32% rain risk in his matchup creates a non-trivial volatility flag that could necessitate a pivot if the forecast deteriorates. **Corbin Carroll** (52.12) and **Gabriel Moreno** (43.72) face a formidable challenge against Kyle Harrison, and while both remain in the starting lineup to chase stolen base upside, their output will be heavily dependent on their ability to work counts against a high-skill arm. **Trevor Story** remains sidelined on the IL, while **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** are held in reserve to manage our game caps effectively.",
